== (2) the engine curve ==
  A = u³·γ(x/u) with γ(s) = (1, 3s, −s³): [0, 0, 0] (zero ⟹ verified)
  γ'×γ'' = [-18*s, 0, 0]  — vanishes at s=0 ⟹ CUSP at s=0:
  the engine is a CUSPIDAL CUBIC (projectively unique class).

== (3) unification: the variant-radical examples' engines ==
  radical 1+(-2)xy: det[A_x,A_y,A] = 0; P(A) = [1 : 3s : −s³] with s = x/(1+-2xy) — same cuspidal cubic
  radical 1+(3)xy: det[A_x,A_y,A] = 0; P(A) = [1 : 3s : −s³] with s = x/(1+3xy) — same cuspidal cubic

== (4) which engine curves are allowed? line and conic engines ==
  line engine A=(1,x,0): condition (1) det = 0 (auto-satisfied)
  then det[B_x,B_y,A] = Derivative(B2(x, y), x)*Derivative(B3(x, y), y) - Derivative(B2(x, y), y)*Derivative(B3(x, y), x)
